  abstract={A dual-band, dual-polarised patch antenna is proposed for SWIPT applications in IoT sensor networks supporting Industry $\text{5.0}$ systems. It operates at $\text{3.3 - 4.9 ~ GHz}$ for data and 5.2 GHz for power transfer. The design utilises a proximity-coupled feed and a pixelated capacitive coupling structure to enable direct RF-to-DC rectification without the need for external matching circuits. The antenna achieves a 46.3 % impedance bandwidth and maintains stable dual-polarised performance under varying environmental conditions. Simulations in CST Studio Suite show a peak RF-to-DC conversion efficiency of 56.5 % over an input power range of -15 to 10 dBm. Compared to conventional SWIPT designs with a baseline efficiency of $\text{45 \%}$, this reflects a $\text{25 \%}$ improvement. The proposed antenna provides a scalable and efficient solution for wideband SWIPT integration in self-sustaining IoT sensor systems.},
